#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119661 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119847 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "be3d5a74-259e-58b9-948d-47ba7412ab08" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Rank of a Matrix Given the Number of Pivot Columns"}] :question/id #uuid "7cce27e9-e2b2-599c-9f4e-437caf1a23ae" :question/math-academy-id "e-5415" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $4 \\times 7$ matrix that has $3$ **non-pivot** columns. Find $\\textrm{rank}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\textrm{rank}(A)$ is the number of pivot columns in $A$. \n\nSince $A$ has $7$ columns and $3$ of them are non-pivots, then the number of pivot columns in $A$ is \n\n$$\n7-3=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{rank}(A)=4$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119662 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d847ec9-c379-5013-ab77-a9b92dc8ca27" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Matrix With a Given Rank by Inspection"}] :question/id #uuid "a6a3db41-6033-537a-bc9d-03fde02dc869" :question/math-academy-id "e-5417" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $4?$\n\n![](images/2c/2cd43e61d4c51ee86d78217688daea5f8ebdfa656a9628e4bef3ef4ac9f8bd3a.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that a matrix of rank $4$ must have at least $4$ columns and at least $4$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $B$ since it has only $3$ rows. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $4$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $A$ has only $3$ pivot columns, while the matrix $C$ has exactly $4$ pivot columns. So, $\\textrm{rank}(A)=3$ and $\\textrm{rank}(C)=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119663 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119849 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f5a44c9-16e5-55fb-a10f-15435a0a9a4c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank of a Matrix Using Row Reduction"}] :question/id #uuid "b3e4eb01-0669-586b-a716-aef87d1c3580" :question/math-academy-id "e-5418" :question/problem "If ![](images/82/823965b7b8f818ec843aefc4c4cc16ef2922e269db8d53f37cf633ff132e5783.svg), find $\\textrm{rank}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the rank of $A,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 35\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has $3$ pivot columns (or, alternatively, it has exactly $3$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{rank}(A)=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d847ec9-c379-5013-ab77-a9b92dc8ca27" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Matrix With a Given Rank by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e848c5c-571a-5e64-9774-00d01483c1b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269840} {:answer/id #uuid "485053f7-0cf4-5064-9d78-fece029c1309" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269927} {:answer/id #uuid "6acd1ef8-2f92-53fa-839e-17421947db6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270219} {:answer/id #uuid "b35756ef-2a37-53f6-aa1c-401e085a1191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270868} {:answer/id #uuid "be5abba8-20d9-50e9-9f16-0ed198ebf305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be5abba8-20d9-50e9-9f16-0ed198ebf305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270950} :answer-field/id #uuid "90a5144d-5b7f-5cb0-877a-bcc5df428d43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b3d88d7-df58-5328-a9cc-5e2d9def75f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-139958" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices has a rank of $4?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that a matrix of rank $4$ must have at least $4$ columns and at least $4$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the following matrices:\n\n- $A$ since it has only $2$ rows.\n\n- $B$ since it has only $3$  rows.\n\n- $D$ since it has only $3$ columns.\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $4$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $C$ has exactly $4$ pivot columns, while the matrix $E$ has only $3$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=4$ and $\\text{rank}(E)=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the matrix $C.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425059 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119849 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f5a44c9-16e5-55fb-a10f-15435a0a9a4c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank of a Matrix Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14c4ed15-45f5-58b1-8360-553b48f39d3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425010} {:answer/id #uuid "3f6df2aa-3a3c-5b79-95be-3aa1251322e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425017} {:answer/id #uuid "50ede2f9-25a2-5752-be09-6a03468fd702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425021} {:answer/id #uuid "b3662759-0a3a-5444-ae02-4e604c768bf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425035} {:answer/id #uuid "d0c17d6f-b6f3-5934-a787-839b47f6354b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f6df2aa-3a3c-5b79-95be-3aa1251322e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425017} :answer-field/id #uuid "53d401b7-f4a5-53bf-90cd-e38c287d2cd7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425047}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a35aea07-c94b-5a19-9d28-82b8ec3131d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-139966" :question/problem "If \n$W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -6 & 4 & -7\\end{aligned}]$, then $\\text{rank}(W)=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the rank of $H,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -6 & 4 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $3$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(W)=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425055 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119849 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f5a44c9-16e5-55fb-a10f-15435a0a9a4c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank of a Matrix Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b20e34e-3de9-55a2-9483-aacb5be32d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425008} {:answer/id #uuid "17628bca-0c14-5472-acd0-2fe108d7530a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425012} {:answer/id #uuid "4508060c-7fe7-5a16-bd3e-18d84d0901d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425018} {:answer/id #uuid "70622a79-c9d6-529b-9225-ebaa52284a66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425026} {:answer/id #uuid "7d77b117-d7d3-56fe-b224-a19869996959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425030}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b20e34e-3de9-55a2-9483-aacb5be32d8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425008} :answer-field/id #uuid "70236281-7f70-52d0-841b-4b25aab4bef3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "06e82198-39dc-5c74-b637-e63de9108225" :question/math-academy-id "q-34763" :question/problem "If $D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,$ then $\\text{rank}(D)=$" :question/worked-solution "To find the rank of $D,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $3$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(D)=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119847 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "be3d5a74-259e-58b9-948d-47ba7412ab08" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Rank of a Matrix Given the Number of Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b97f7fb-f59f-5b80-a935-c68290aa5e39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425009} {:answer/id #uuid "26b3bf8f-7cf5-524b-a85f-d2a316221c81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425014} {:answer/id #uuid "6de902b4-92d9-5e7e-a47b-a566c29a3f3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425025} {:answer/id #uuid "a18d2568-e5ef-5a54-ad1b-469416888c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425031} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b09269-ca4b-585c-8c78-317ce11f315d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425036}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26b3bf8f-7cf5-524b-a85f-d2a316221c81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425014} :answer-field/id #uuid "757ae7be-4c48-52a1-bebe-15d0b1ed0f1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425051}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6826463c-847d-5512-b760-3fbeb596f635" :question/math-academy-id "q-34805" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $7\\times 12$ matrix that has $6$ **pivot** columns. What is the rank of the matrix?" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\text{rank}(A)$ is the number of pivot columns in $A.$ \n\nSince we are told that $A$ has $6$ pivot columns, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)=6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120363 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119847 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "be3d5a74-259e-58b9-948d-47ba7412ab08" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Rank of a Matrix Given the Number of Pivot Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "253bc858-812c-5e74-983b-cd0de2eb0f22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317682} {:answer/id #uuid "2a24cb2d-1445-54a0-bacf-08246573e89a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317695} {:answer/id #uuid "334787ce-0a56-588a-a4c8-8b58eecb9d69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317729} {:answer/id #uuid "6e8b9422-7271-5c25-b890-90a23aa7d66e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317949} {:answer/id #uuid "be4b1522-823c-5a19-916d-dd2b3e04a7aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/valu